    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4643" root="ثلث" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثَلِّثٌ</span></b>  <i>A calumniator,</i> or <i>slanderer, of his brother</i>
[or <i>fellow</i>] <i>to his prince;</i> because he destroys three;
namely, himself and his brother and his prince:
(Sh, T, M, * K:) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثْلِثٌ</span></b> ; (K;) or thus
accord. to Aboo-'Owáneh. (Sh, T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثِلْثٌ</span>, last sentence: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَلُوثٌ</span>.

